-- title:
--   Grothendieck’s bounded-disk expansion with scalar tensor factor
-- statement:
--   Let G be a complete Hausdorff nuclear locally convex space which is either Fréchet or of type (DF). For each bounded subset B of G there is a sequence y_n converging to zero in G, a nonnegative summable sequence c_n, and linear functionals a_n on the algebraic span of B. Every x in that span has the convergent expansion x = Σ a_n(x)y_n, and for each x in B the simultaneous bounds |a_n(x)| ≤ c_n hold. The functionals depend linearly on x and the envelope is uniform over B.
--
--   This is the scalar specialization of Grothendieck's bounded-disk expansion theorem. Take the second tensor factor to be the scalar field, which is of both indicated types. Completeness identifies the completed projective tensor product with G. Apply Theorem 5 to the closed absolutely convex hull A of B. Its disk norm gives norm at most one to points of B. Equicontinuity on the normed space generated by A bounds all of the source's coefficient functionals uniformly on B. Restrict them to the span of B and absorb the source's summable scalar weights into the functionals to obtain a_n and c_n. The assertion asks for an actual series in G, simultaneously for the entire span.
-- source:
--   A. Grothendieck, Résumé des résultats essentiels dans la théorie des produits tensoriels topologiques et des espaces nucléaires, Annales de l’Institut Fourier 4 (1952), pp. 73–112, §2.4, Theorem 5, p. 104. Scalar-factor specialization F=ℂ. https://doi.org/10.5802/aif.46

import Definitions.Def_MasulloGRH_LocallyConvex

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace MasulloGRH

theorem bounded_disk_scalar_expansion (G : Type*) [AddCommGroup G] [Module ℂ G]
    [TopologicalSpace G] (hC : IsCompleteTVS G) (hN : IsNuclear G)
    (hclass : IsFrechet G ∨
      ((∃ B : ℕ → Set G, (∀ n, Bornology.IsVonNBounded ℂ (B n)) ∧
      ∀ S : Set G, Bornology.IsVonNBounded ℂ S → ∃ n, S ⊆ B n) ∧
       (∀ U : ℕ → Set G, (∀ n, U n ∈ nhds (0 : G) ∧ IsClosed (U n) ∧ Balanced ℂ (U n) ∧ Convex ℝ (U n)) →
      (∀ S : Set G, Bornology.IsVonNBounded ℂ S → Absorbs ℂ (⋂ n, U n) S) →
      (⋂ n, U n) ∈ nhds (0 : G))))
    (B : Set G) (hBb : Bornology.IsVonNBounded ℂ B) :
    ∃ (y : ℕ → G) (c : ℕ → ℝ) (a : ℕ → (Submodule.span ℂ B) →ₗ[ℂ] ℂ),
      Filter.Tendsto y Filter.atTop (nhds (0 : G)) ∧
      (∀ n, 0 ≤ c n) ∧ Summable c ∧
      (∀ n (x : Submodule.span ℂ B), (x : G) ∈ B → ‖a n x‖ ≤ c n) ∧
      ∀ x : Submodule.span ℂ B, HasSum (fun n => a n x • y n) (x : G) := by sorry

end MasulloGRH
